{"agent_id":"6Vw9","agent_seq":46,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T02:28:35.724435440Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a190982e-4ba5-4a24-b5cb-0f40f38d1e24","title":"Crosslink PostToolUse hook times out running cargo clippy","description":"The generated .crosslink/integrations/hooks/post-edit-check.py treats only agent.json role=agent or provider worktree paths as agent context. This repository's active Crosslink identity has role=driver, so every Rust Write/Edit enters the non-agent branch and synchronously runs cargo clippy with subprocess timeout=30s. Claude's generated .claude/settings.json gives that PostToolUse hook only timeout=5s, causing 'PostToolUse hook (failed): hook timed out after 5s'. crosslink workflow diff confirms the hook matches the shipped default, so this is not local hook drift. Fix should keep PostToolUse bounded below the provider budget: do not run project-wide clippy synchronously, or correctly recognize managed driver sessions and defer heavyweight validation.","priority":"high","created_by":"6Vw9"},"signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBVBXKSNk6DQ8HXUuuNVinRQU9Vlj+IvpFwV8Xdv07e2XdgXQbjqVEP2n75K1HAJ4yCHrS/Usy+5VHY8msVFEQg="}
{"agent_id":"6Vw9","agent_seq":47,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T02:54:41.968975539Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fb1e430f-9423-4e10-9e49-02882a457227","title":"Permission receipt store directory sync is not portable to Windows","description":"S-017 review found save_state unconditionally opens and syncs the parent directory. std::fs::File::open(directory) is not portable to Windows, so an otherwise successful trusted approval write can report failure there. Guard directory fsync to supported Unix targets and add a regression-level source/platform contract.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"5cabfc3b-d756-4c81-8b55-08fec79cd65d","created_by":"6Vw9"},"signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBD8O9ni8xhSNteR7+sEjSW6wES/NuUDk9Yy1Xwt6cqGLKlrRnbatcfrzDX/oEkV0t19W/N91qIqIcDSneLnXAw="}
{"agent_id":"6Vw9","agent_seq":48,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T02:56:15.116591634Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6c9fe694-8efe-4e52-ac24-02922ceae8a9","title":"Tool caps count denied calls and race past configured limits","description":"S-017 authorization audit found ToolExecutor calls check_and_record_tool before permission authorization, so permission-denied calls consume enterprise quota. PolicyEnforcer also performs check and increment under separate mutex acquisitions, allowing concurrent calls to exceed a cap. Move recording after successful exact authorization, keep an early dry-run check, and make capped increment atomic. ACP must pass policy into the shared executor instead of recording before its normalized authorization.","priority":"critical","parent_uuid":"5cabfc3b-d756-4c81-8b55-08fec79cd65d","created_by":"6Vw9"},"signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKziuogptMSyQOJx1sBNVpbS2ORG8Mij8V+14ZpLqmElMsPtUjbFYj5QrfiAz1MAvR3fUzVilXBgJNhpEeQHWQg="}
